1
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:43,142
Bob Lazar: Area 51 and Flying Saucers is a documentary film
directed by Jeremy Kenyon Lockyer Corbell.

2
00:09:14,285 --> 00:09:20,285
Area 51, flying saucers from another world - and the
program to create a fierce technology.

3
00:13:51,428 --> 00:13:57,428
Bob Lazar remains the singular most famous and
controversial name in the world of UFOs.

4
00:18:28,571 --> 00:18:34,571
The reason you know about Area 51 is because Lazar
came forward and told you about it.

5
00:23:05,714 --> 00:23:11,714
His disclosures have turned his life upside-down and he
has tried to stay out of the spotlight.

6
00:27:42,857 --> 00:27:48,857
For this reason, he has never let any filmmaker into the private
world of his daily life - that is - until now.

7
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Corbell’s film explores Lazar’s claims through the lens of thirty years - providing rare and
never before revealed footage - guaranteed to alter the landscape of the debate.

8
00:36:57,142 --> 00:37:03,142
Self - Interviewee, played by Bob Lazar.

9
00:41:34,285 --> 00:41:40,285
Self - Investigative Reporter, played by George Knapp.

10
00:46:11,428 --> 00:46:17,428
Self - The Narrator (voice), played by Mickey Rourke.

11
00:50:48,571 --> 00:50:54,571
Self - Investigative Filmmaker, played by Jeremy Kenyon Lockyer Corbell.

12
00:55:25,714 --> 00:55:31,714
Self - The Wife, played by Joy White.

13
01:00:02,857 --> 01:00:08,857
Self - The Mom, played by Phyllis Tucker.

14
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
Robert Scott Lazar () is an American who, since 1989, has claimed to have been part of a classified US government project concerned with the reverse engineering of
extraterrestrial technology; he also purported to have read government briefing documents that described alien involvement in human affairs over the past 10,000 years.

15
01:09:17,142 --> 01:09:23,142
A self-proclaimed physicist, Lazar supposedly worked at a secret site near the
United States Air Force facility popularly known as Area 51.

16
01:13:54,285 --> 01:14:00,285
His story brought additional public attention to the facility and spawned conspiracy
theories regarding government knowledge of extraterrestrial life.

17
01:18:31,428 --> 01:18:37,428
Lazar has provided no evidence of alien life or technology, and his claims about
his education and employment history are replete with fabrications.

18
01:23:08,571 --> 01:23:14,571
Lazar also has been involved in criminal activity: he was convicted in 1990 for his involvement in a Nevada prostitution ring, and his
company was sentenced to probation in 2006 for violating laws prohibiting the sale of chemicals across state lines.

19
01:27:45,714 --> 01:27:51,714
As well as being dismissed by skeptics, Lazar has
been denounced by some ufologists.

20
01:32:22,857 --> 01:32:28,857
The film explores themes of spacecraft, government, flying saucer, alien, ufo.
